@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+# WCAG verification
+
+The matrix's automated check score is the fraction of automated passes and failures. It is not a conformance score. The WCAG verification panel separately tracks all 50 WCAG 2.1 Level A/AA criteria for every listed page.
+
+Reviewers first define the full-page boundaries, complete processes and interaction states, and platform release/configuration. Each criterion has a specific checklist. Saving evidence requires a current source/rendered fingerprint, scope version, test environment, detailed results, completed checklist and reviewer confirmation. Optional HTTPS links attach external evidence artifacts. Not-applicable outcomes require a reason. The server records the authenticated reviewer and timestamp; clients cannot supply them. Records are append-only. Work-queue verification is task progress and does not sign off WCAG criteria.
+
+`GET /api/v1/project/:projectID/accessibility/workqueue/conformance` supplies the scoped report. POST actions at `/conformance/scope`, `/conformance/review`, and `/conformance/signoff` require project editing permission. They share the work queue's authentication and authorization. The report includes page URLs, scanner evidence, versions, reviewer results, scope, sign-off and limitations. Export is available while pending, with pending status intact.
+
+Rendered scans run through `/page/:sectionID/rendered-scan`, which resolves the URL from the authorized project's stored section. Source and rendered hashes must match. Missing/failed/incomplete resource loads, missing criteria, automated failures, stale scans (24 hours), unreviewed or failed criteria and stale scope/content/platform evidence block sign-off. A scan pass or legal exception cannot establish WCAG conformance. Full-page findings are labeled for developer review in the work queue and are not automatically writable.
+
+A reviewer can sign only after all criteria for all listed pages are current and verified. The statement binds to a digest of scope, page fingerprints and review records. Scope/content/rendering changes invalidate it. Exported reports are dated evidence snapshots, not promises about future content or a third-party certification. Changes outside the application are detected on rescan; scan freshness limits this gap.
+
+Human tests must cover mathematical meaning and navigability, duplicate announcements, keyboard interaction, zoom/reflow/text spacing, media and complex images, linguistic accuracy, and the complete reader processes defined in scope. Never auto-populate these results from AI inference or axe checks.
